# Bloodline SEO Rules

## Core SEO Philosophy

SEO should feel:

- premium
- authoritative
- trust-heavy
- region-aware
- conversion-oriented

Avoid:
- keyword stuffing
- thin SEO pages
- AI spam content
- doorway page patterns
- cheap local SEO tactics

---

## Metadata Rules

Use centralized metadata generation.

Use:
- `generateMetadata`
- shared SEO helpers
- typed metadata systems

Avoid:
- duplicated metadata logic
- hardcoded metadata everywhere
- inconsistent title structures

---

## Title Rules

Preferred patterns:

```txt
{Topic} in {Region} | Bloodline Tattoo
```

Examples:

```txt
Realistic Tattoos in Bangkok | Bloodline Tattoo
Cover-Up Tattoos in Bali | Bloodline Tattoo
```

Titles should:
- remain readable
- support trust
- support SEO naturally

Avoid:
- keyword repetition
- spammy title formatting

---

## Meta Description Rules

Descriptions should:
- sound human
- reinforce trust
- support conversion
- include regional context naturally

Avoid:
- robotic phrasing
- excessive keyword stuffing
- generic AI wording

---

## Canonical Rules

Each regional domain canonicalizes to itself.

Correct:

```txt
Bangkok pages
→ Bangkok canonical

Bali pages
→ Bali canonical
```

Avoid:
- forcing canonicals to global domain
- cross-region canonical confusion

---

## Regional SEO Rules

Every regional page should contain:
- region-aware metadata
- localized reviews
- localized schema
- localized FAQ variation
- localized supporting copy

Avoid:
- cloned regional pages
- duplicate regional content
- copy-pasted SEO structures

---

## Heading Hierarchy Rules

Maintain:

- one H1 only
- logical H2 hierarchy
- logical H3 progression

Headings should:
- remain semantic
- remain readable
- support scanning

Avoid:
- multiple H1s
- decorative heading misuse
- keyword stuffing in headings

---

## Internal Linking Rules

Internal linking is mandatory.

Pages should support:
- style ↔ service links
- blog ↔ style links
- blog ↔ service links
- gallery ↔ styles
- FAQ ↔ services

Links should feel:
- contextual
- useful
- natural

Avoid:
- spammy link blocks
- repetitive exact-match anchors

---

## Anchor Text Rules

Anchor text should:
- describe destination naturally
- support user discovery
- support SEO context

Avoid:
- exact-match repetition loops
- manipulative anchor spam

---

## Schema Rules

Use centralized schema utilities.

Supported schema:

- LocalBusiness
- TattooParlor
- FAQPage
- Article
- BreadcrumbList
- Review
- AggregateRating

Do not fabricate schema data.

---

## Review SEO Rules

Reviews should:
- remain crawlable
- remain authentic
- remain region-aware

Avoid:
- fake testimonials
- fabricated ratings
- duplicated reviews across regions

---

## MDX SEO Rules

MDX content should:
- maintain heading hierarchy
- include internal links
- support topical authority
- remain human-readable
- reinforce trust

Avoid:
- filler paragraphs
- repetitive AI structures
- keyword spam sections

---

## Content Density Rules

The platform supports:
- long-form SEO
- FAQs
- educational content

BUT content must remain:
- structured
- scannable
- visually readable

Avoid:
- giant text walls
- bloated SEO copy
- meaningless filler sections

---

## Blog Rules

Blog content should support:
- topical authority
- tattoo education
- traveler intent
- conversion nurturing

Avoid:
- generic marketing blogs
- mass AI article generation
- low-information content

---

## FAQ Rules

FAQs should:
- answer real user concerns
- support long-tail SEO
- reduce conversion friction

Avoid:
- fake FAQ stuffing
- bloated repetitive answers

---

## Image SEO Rules

All meaningful images require:
- descriptive alt text
- optimized filenames
- responsive sizing

Avoid:
- keyword-stuffed alt text
- meaningless alt content

---

## Gallery SEO Rules

Gallery is a:
```txt
visual authority system
```

Gallery content should:
- support style categorization
- support internal linking
- support SEO naturally

Avoid:
- unstructured media dumps

---

## Performance SEO Rules

SEO-critical pages should prioritize:
- Server Components
- ISR
- optimized media
- low hydration cost
- fast LCP

Avoid:
- client-rendered SEO content
- oversized animation payloads
- runtime-heavy pages

---

## Route SEO Rules

Approved SEO route groups:

```txt
tattoo-styles/
tattoo-services/
tattoo-blog/
gallery/
reviews/
faq/
```

Do not invent:
- doorway city pages
- thin keyword routes
- duplicate route intent

---

## AI Content Rules

AI-generated content must:
- feel human
- remain trustworthy
- avoid repetition
- support expertise
- support topical authority

Avoid:
- generic AI tone
- repetitive sentence patterns
- obvious machine-generated structure

---

## Premium Positioning Rules

SEO must never weaken:
- premium perception
- trust
- craftsmanship positioning
- professional tone

Avoid:
- spammy conversion language
- cheap local SEO tactics
- aggressive keyword repetition

---

## Forbidden SEO Patterns

Never introduce:

- keyword stuffing
- thin pages
- duplicate metadata
- duplicate regional copy
- fake schema
- fake testimonials
- hidden SEO text
- doorway pages
- exact-match anchor spam
- AI filler content

---

## Final Principle

Every SEO decision should reinforce:

- authority
- trust
- craftsmanship
- regional relevance
- premium positioning
- conversion quality
- long-term scalability

If an SEO implementation weakens those goals, do not implement it.